From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yaozhi mpv build <build@local.invalid>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 03:05:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ao_sdl: preserve Windows 5.1.4 and 7.1.4 layouts

SDL2 reports only the obtained channel count to applications.  The generic
SDL output selector therefore reduced explicit layouts above eight channels
to 7.1 before opening the device.  On a 10- or 12-channel WASAPI endpoint,
SDL then expanded that eight-channel stream back to the device channel count,
folding height channels into the bed and leaving some output slots silent.

Whitelist the two spatial layouts whose Windows speaker masks are supplied by
the bundled SDL2 backend.  This keeps mpv's interleaved samples in exact
WAVEFORMATEXTENSIBLE order from the audio filter through SDL:

5.1.4: FL FR FC LFE SL SR TFL TFR TBL TBR
7.1.4: FL FR FC LFE BL BR SL SR TFL TFR TBL TBR
---
 audio/out/ao_sdl.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/audio/out/ao_sdl.c b/audio/out/ao_sdl.c
index 6bc346c11..5e6127955 100644
--- a/audio/out/ao_sdl.c
+++ b/audio/out/ao_sdl.c
@@ -104,6 +104,22 @@ static int init(struct ao *ao)
     }
 
     struct mp_chmap_sel sel = {0};
+#ifdef _WIN32
+    // SDL exposes only a channel count.  Keep these layouts explicit so mpv
+    // does not downmix them to 7.1 before the patched WASAPI backend applies
+    // its matching WAVEFORMATEXTENSIBLE speaker mask.
+    struct mp_chmap spatial_layout;
+    if (mp_chmap_from_str(&spatial_layout,
+                          bstr0("fl-fr-fc-lfe-sl-sr-tfl-tfr-tbl-tbr")))
+    {
+        mp_chmap_sel_add_map(&sel, &spatial_layout);
+    }
+    if (mp_chmap_from_str(&spatial_layout,
+                          bstr0("fl-fr-fc-lfe-bl-br-sl-sr-tfl-tfr-tbl-tbr")))
+    {
+        mp_chmap_sel_add_map(&sel, &spatial_layout);
+    }
+#endif
     mp_chmap_sel_add_waveext_def(&sel);
     if (!ao_chmap_sel_adjust(ao, &sel, &ao->channels)) {
         uninit(ao);
-- 
